/*
  PullToRefresh.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0188 · PullToRefresh (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The first three keys mirror the web source
  (components/mobile/PullToRefresh.tsx) one-for-one — the indicator copy the web `t(...)` calls render
  (`mobile.refresh.pull` / `.release` / `.refreshing`). The `action` / `hint` keys are the native
  VoiceOver affordance: the web pull gesture has no assistive equivalent, so the native port exposes an
  explicit "Refresh" accessibility action with a describing hint. Keeping all copy here means the Swift
  sources hold no English literals.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are
  kept in a per-surface table ("PullToRefresh") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings
  without editing the shared catalog.
*/

/* --- Indicator copy (web `PullToRefresh.tsx`) --- */
"mobile.refresh.pull" = "Pull to refresh";
"mobile.refresh.release" = "Release to refresh";
"mobile.refresh.refreshing" = "Refreshing…";

/* --- Accessibility affordance (native VoiceOver action) --- */
"mobile.refresh.action" = "Refresh";
"mobile.refresh.hint" = "Pull down to refresh";
